<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Raja Ampat Islands</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Raja Ampat Islands are an archipelago off the western tip of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-guinea">New Guinea</a>, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>'s province of Southwest Papua, centred on the islands of Waigeo, Batanta, Salawati and Misool. Their name, meaning 'four kings', recalls local rulers who owed tribute to the Sultanate of Tidore. Today they are known for the exceptional biodiversity of their coral reefs.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/raja-ampat-islands.jpg" alt="Raja Ampat Islands" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jonathan Chase · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Raja_Ampat_Islands_-_journal.pbio.1001457.g001.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
